      "sourceId": "src-cb58364194b432c7",
      "quote": "UC San Diego Lab of Cognitive Imaging Dedicated to the study of Brain-behavioral Relationships We are a group of interdisciplinary imaging scientists dedicated to the study of brain-behavioral relationships in patients with neurological disorders, including epilepsy, brain tumors, and dementia. We use structural, functional, and diffusion imaging in combination with neuropsychological data to predict postsurgical cognitive outcomes. Our Research Explore our current projects including Multimodal Imaging of Cognitive Networks in Epilepsy as well as Prediction of seizure lateralization and postoperative outcome through the use of deep learning applied to multi-site MRI/DTI data: An ENIGMA-Epilepsy study. More information Our People Lab members Collaborators Awards & Highlights Contact Us UC San Diego Lab of Cognitive Imaging 9452 Medical Center Drive Mail Code 0841 La Jolla, CA 92037 LOCIResearch@gmail.com",
